@startuml quotas-limites
!theme plain
title Gestion des quotas et limites de ressources

participant "gandal_deploy.py" as script
participant "API Server" as api
participant "Admission\nController" as admission
participant "Scheduler" as scheduler
database "etcd" as etcd

== Déploiement initial : 2 réplicas ==

script -> api : POST Deployment\n(replicas: 2, no resources specified)
api -> admission : Validate + Mutate
activate admission

admission -> etcd : Read LimitRange (default-limits)
etcd --> admission : default: cpu=500m, memory=512Mi\ndefaultRequest: cpu=100m, memory=128Mi

admission -> admission : Inject default values into pod spec
note right
    Container spec devient:
    resources:
      requests:
        cpu: 100m
        memory: 128Mi
      limits:
        cpu: 500m
        memory: 512Mi
end note

admission -> etcd : Read ResourceQuota (project-quota)
etcd --> admission : hard:\n  pods: 4\n  requests.cpu: 1\n  requests.memory: 1Gi\n  limits.cpu: 2\n  limits.memory: 2Gi

admission -> admission : Calculate current usage + new request
note right
    Current usage: 0
    New request:
      2 pods × 100m CPU = 200m
      2 pods × 128Mi RAM = 256Mi
    
    Total:
      pods: 2 / 4 ✅
      requests.cpu: 200m / 1 ✅
      requests.memory: 256Mi / 1Gi ✅
end note

admission --> api : ✅ Approved
deactivate admission

api -> etcd : Create Deployment
etcd --> api : Created
api -> scheduler : 2 pods Pending
scheduler -> scheduler : Schedule pods
scheduler --> api : Pods scheduled

== Tentative de scale à 10 réplicas ==

script -> api : PATCH Deployment\n(replicas: 10)
api -> etcd : Update Deployment.spec.replicas = 10
etcd --> api : Updated

api -> scheduler : Watch: 8 new pods Pending (total 10)
activate scheduler

scheduler -> api : Request pod creation (3/10)
api -> admission : Validate pod
activate admission

admission -> etcd : Read ResourceQuota
etcd --> admission : Current usage:\n  pods: 2\n  requests.cpu: 200m\n  requests.memory: 256Mi

admission -> admission : Calculate: current + new
note right
    New request for 8 pods:
      8 × 100m = 800m CPU
      8 × 128Mi = 1024Mi RAM
    
    Total would be:
      pods: 10 / 4 ❌ EXCEEDED
      requests.cpu: 1000m / 1000m ✅
      requests.memory: 1280Mi / 1Gi ❌ EXCEEDED
end note

admission --> api : ❌ REJECTED\nQuota exceeded
deactivate admission

api -> etcd : Create Event\nReason: FailedCreate\nMessage: exceeded quota
scheduler -[#red]x api : Cannot create pod

note right
    Le Deployment reste à
    replicas=10 dans la spec,
    mais seulement 4 pods
    sont créés (2 existants + 2 nouveaux)
end note

scheduler -> api : Request pod creation (4/10)
api -> admission : Validate pod
admission -> admission : Calculate: 4 pods total
note right
    pods: 4 / 4 ✅ (limite atteinte)
    requests.cpu: 400m / 1 ✅
    requests.memory: 512Mi / 1Gi ✅
end note
admission --> api : ✅ Approved (dernier pod autorisé)
deactivate scheduler

== État final ==

script -> api : GET Deployment status
api -> etcd : Read Deployment
etcd --> api : spec.replicas: 10\nstatus.replicas: 4\nstatus.readyReplicas: 4

api --> script : Status: 4/10 ready
note right
    Le cluster a créé le maximum
    de pods autorisés par le quota
end note

script -> api : GET Events
api -> etcd : List events
etcd --> api : Events with reason=FailedCreate
api --> script : "exceeded quota: project-quota"

script --> script : ✅ Test 5 passed:\nQuota respected, scale limited

== Diagramme des limites ==

rectangle "ResourceQuota: project-quota" as quota {
    rectangle "Pods: 4 / 4" as pods #pink
    rectangle "CPU requests: 400m / 1" as cpu_req #lightgreen
    rectangle "Memory requests: 512Mi / 1Gi" as mem_req #lightgreen
    rectangle "CPU limits: 2 / 2" as cpu_lim #lightgreen
    rectangle "Memory limits: 2Gi / 2Gi" as mem_lim #lightgreen
}

rectangle "LimitRange: default-limits" as limitrange {
    rectangle "Default CPU: 500m" as default_cpu
    rectangle "Default Memory: 512Mi" as default_mem
    rectangle "Default Request CPU: 100m" as req_cpu
    rectangle "Default Request Memory: 128Mi" as req_mem
}

note bottom of quota
    Le quota limite le **total**
    des ressources du namespace
end note

note bottom of limitrange
    Le LimitRange injecte des
    valeurs par défaut si non spécifiées
end note

legend right
    |= État | Couleur |
    | <#lightgreen> En dessous | Vert |
    | <#pink> Limite atteinte | Rose |
    | <#red> Dépassement | Rouge (rejeté) |
    
    **Comportement:**
    1. LimitRange injecte les valeurs par défaut
    2. Admission Controller vérifie le quota
    3. Si quota dépassé → rejet du pod
    4. Le Deployment reste à replicas=10 (état désiré)
    5. Seulement 4 pods sont créés (état réel)
    6. Events "FailedCreate" générés
endlegend

@enduml
